{"version":"1","id":"sqlshack","handle":"sqlshack","name":"SQL Shack","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/7b6468c7be7a4bb78461bce41bcb2dd3","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-1.9224,"y":-2.5629,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":300,"newest_post_at":"2024-09-21T11:17:47.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-09-15T12:27:51.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.01,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":6.596667,"summary_length_avg":341.996656,"title_length_avg":50.56,"title_length_var":237.179733,"tag_entropy":2.991398,"tag_diversity":0.283333,"top_tag_share":0.176667,"avg_upvotes":1.113333,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.033333,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.032836,"zero_engagement_share":0.73,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":1.905717,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.010101},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-3.0882,-0.0441],"cadence_depth":[5.6324,1.5588],"hype_variety":[-4.9706,-2.1912],"title_style":[-4.9559,3.0147]},"top_tags":[["sql",185],["microsoft-sql-server",164],["azure",113],["general-programming",85],["database",78],["postgresql",33],["backend",25],["storage",19]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["5 Best Practices for writing SQL queries","Difference between SQL SELECT UNIQUE and SELECT DISTINCT","PostgreSQL Tutorial for beginners"],"outlier":["How to identify suitable SKUs for Azure SQL Database, Managed Instance (MI), or SQL Server on Azure VM"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"0CVvkHBR3","title":"Understanding PostgreSQL SUBSTRING function","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/understanding-postgresql-substring-function/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/understanding-postgresql-substring-function-0cvvkhbr3","summary":"PostgreSQL, an open-source relational database system, provides several string manipulation functions, including the SUBSTRING function. The SUBSTRING function is used to extract a part of a string based on a specified starting position and, optionally, the length. This guide covers the syntax and various examples of using the SUBSTRING function, including using regular expressions and extracting data from table columns. Additional features and scenarios for using the function, such as sorting data and handling email addresses, are also explored.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5b16c52075a47ce95b9242eff9eabb31?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-21T11:17:47.000Z"},{"id":"UrGk53ESJ","title":"How to create and query the Python PostgreSQL database","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/how-to-create-and-query-the-python-postgresql-database/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-create-and-query-the-python-postgresql-database-urgk53esj","summary":"Learn how to create and query a PostgreSQL database using Python. This guide is suitable for both beginners and professionals and covers setting up the environment, connecting to the database, and manipulating database objects using Python. Steps include installing PostgreSQL, configuring Visual Studio Code, and using psycopg2 for database interactions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fa4467500d12279c8fdc959692eb3761?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-08-15T10:53:58.000Z"},{"id":"PEjTaONw3","title":"Different ways to identify and change compatibility levels in SQL Server","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/different-ways-to-identify-and-change-compatibility-levels-in-sql-server/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/different-ways-to-identify-and-change-compatibility-levels-in-sql-server-pejtaonw3","summary":"Compatibility level in SQL Server is a property that determines how the database behaves in terms of syntax and query optimization, allowing for backward compatibility with older versions. Methods to identify and change the compatibility level include using dynamic management views and SQL Server Management Studio, as well as executing the ALTER DATABASE command. New features introduced with different compatibility levels include Query Store, Intelligent Query Processing, and Temporal Tables, among others.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/45efa340974a9a6e5d53864a63211c64?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-22T10:00:15.000Z"},{"id":"4kDs42FBw","title":"Oracle Substring function overview with examples","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/oracle-substring-function-overview-with-examples/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/oracle-substring-function-overview-with-examples-4kds42fbw","summary":"Learn how to set up an Oracle instance on AWS and use the Oracle SUBSTRING function to extract specific portions of text from data. The process includes setting up the database instance on AWS RDS, configuring it, and using an IDE like DBeaver to run queries. Detailed examples demonstrate how to apply the SUBSTRING function to both static text and data structures within the database.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f1d32cd5190ecc04b32c5a289e372fed?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-19T13:45:50.000Z"},{"id":"VPeB4w1iy","title":"Configure backup storage redundancy for Azure Cosmos DB account","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/configure-backup-storage-redundancy-for-azure-cosmos-db-account/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/configure-backup-storage-redundancy-for-azure-cosmos-db-account-vpeb4w1iy","summary":"Learn about backup storage redundancy for Azure Cosmos DB and how to change it for an existing account.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/73e1677605ce0a40da6f3c31eb7fa62f?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-15T13:30:00.000Z"},{"id":"A7s38V1EL","title":"SQL Performance Tuning tips for newbies","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/sql-performance-tuning-tips-for-newbies/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sql-performance-tuning-tips-for-newbies-a7s38v1el","summary":"This post provides basic advice for SQL performance tuning, including enabling and viewing time statistics, interpreting query execution plans, staying updated on new features, and using tools like sp_whoisactive, Extended Events, and Query Store.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/652fdf73a65948d14a99b595d079e451?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-15T12:12:47.000Z"},{"id":"QDF6sF2H7","title":"Understanding the SQL IN operator with examples","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/understanding-the-sql-in-operator-with-examples/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/understanding-the-sql-in-operator-with-examples-qdf6sf2h7","summary":"Learn about the SQL IN operator, its syntax and parameters, and how it works with strings, numbers, and dates. Replace multiple OR conditions with the IN operator. Use the IN operator with subqueries and nested IN operators. Understand the concept of duplicate values and the NOT IN operator. Examples provided.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c18f4e84c904619310bb633781868158?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-19T10:36:10.000Z"},{"id":"Zcs2mmthU","title":"Finding Duplicates in SQL","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/finding-duplicates-in-sql/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/finding-duplicates-in-sql-zcs2mmthu","summary":"This post explains the different ways to find duplicate values in SQL using DISTINCT and COUNT, GROUP BY and COUNT, and ROW_NUMBER functions. It provides examples and guidance on how to use these functions to identify duplicates in single columns or across multiple columns. The post also highlights the importance of managing duplicates in data storage and processing.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8a66f2c22f05beeed4b09cb978d9e429?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":23,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-07T10:57:43.000Z"},{"id":"EEXSTw7DD","title":"Difference between SQL SELECT UNIQUE and SELECT DISTINCT","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/difference-between-sql-select-unique-and-select-distinct/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/difference-between-sql-select-unique-and-select-distinct-eexstw7dd","summary":"Learn about the difference between SQL SELECT UNIQUE and SELECT DISTINCT, the use of UNIQUE constraint, and the syntax for executing these statements in Oracle. Both statements are used to fetch unique values from a column that may have duplicate values.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c1e024bf7dd56ba3d18327d22f1ff88b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":28,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-01-16T10:28:26.000Z"},{"id":"TZjqxJCN3","title":"An overview of SQL Server monitoring tools","url":"https://www.sqlshack.com/an-overview-of-sql-server-monitoring-tools/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/an-overview-of-sql-server-monitoring-tools-tzjqxjcn3","summary":"This article provides an overview of SQL Server monitoring tools and techniques, including SQL Server Profiler, SQL Server Extended Events, SQL Server Management Studio Reports, SQL Server Management Studio Activity Monitor, dynamic management views and functions, Windows Resources Monitor, and third-party tools. It explains the importance of database monitoring and highlights the availability of free and commercial tools for SQL Server monitoring.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9a7f5356ad1aa8e3b195738624fb6538?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-12T14:43:54.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["stuffandnonsense","vikingsoftware","shopifychangelog","randomascii","equinix"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"stuffandnonsense","handle":"stuff